      {
        "data": {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Five tools cover most needs in 2026: Remini (best known as a phone app), MyHeritage Photo Enhancer (part of a genealogy platform), VanceAI (professional multi-tool suite), Magic Memory (GFPGAN, web-first, one-time credits), and Fotor (general photo editor with AI enhancement). Together they span one-off family photos to batch professional jobs.",
              },
              "name": "What are the most popular AI photo restoration tools in 2026?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Magic Memory has no free tier: restorations use one-time credits from €9.99 for 20, and a failed restoration costs no credit. Of the others, VanceAI gives 10 credits to try, Fotor has a free Basic plan with limited credits, and MyHeritage has free sign-up but does not publish a free-use limit.",
              },
              "name": "What is the best free AI photo restoration tool in 2026?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Magic Memory's €29.99 / 120-credit pack works out to €0.25 per photo, and €9.99 buys 20 photos; credits never expire. Remini and MyHeritage sell recurring subscriptions, so their cost per photo depends on how many photos you restore before you cancel.",
              },
              "name": "What is the cheapest AI photo restoration for 20+ photos?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "All five work in a web browser, so you can restore a photo without installing anything. Remini, MyHeritage, and Fotor also have mobile apps.",
              },
              "name": "Which tool works without downloading an app?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Across the top tools, the common features are face-specific restoration (sharper eyes, recovered skin texture, repaired teeth/hair detail), upscaling (output at 2x or 4x the input resolution), and damage repair (scratches, tears, fading). Higher-tier tools additionally offer colorization of black-and-white photos, batch processing, and integration with family-tree or social-media workflows. The single most important differentiator is whether the model is face-specialized (GFPGAN-based) or general-purpose.",
              },
              "name": "What are the features of popular AI photo restoration tools?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes. The restored photo you download is a permanent image file. It does not degrade or change after you download it. Save multiple copies in different locations for long-term preservation.",
              },
              "name": "Are AI photo restoration results permanent?",
            },
          ],
        },
        "sha256": "f100b100783fb4fae57a1391874db7554090932dd5a8e5ae7bf62d6bd8a9336a",
      },
    ],
