      {
        "data": {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No. Magic Memory uses one-time credit packages — not a subscription. You pay once, use the credits whenever you want, and they never expire. Competitors like Remini charge a weekly, monthly or yearly subscription; you can buy 20 Magic Memory credits for €9.99 and keep them forever.",
              },
              "name": "Is Magic Memory a subscription?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Paid credits never expire. Once you buy a Starter, Growth, or Premium pack, those restorations stay in your account until you use them — no monthly deadline, no forced renewal.",
              },
              "name": "Do my credits ever expire?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "If you have a few photos or a batch of up to 20 family photos to get through, Starter (20 credits for €9.99) is the cheapest per-photo option for small projects. Growth (60 credits for €19.99, €0.33 per restoration) covers a full album. Premium (120 credits for €29.99, €0.25 per restoration) is best for photographers, genealogists, or anyone digitizing decades of prints.",
              },
              "name": "Which plan is right for me?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "The per-restoration cost drops as you buy larger packs. Starter: €0.50/photo. Growth: €0.33/photo. Premium: €0.25/photo. You pay once, there is no subscription to cancel, and credits never expire.",
              },
              "name": "How much does each restoration cost?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Magic Memory is based in the EU, so we price in Euros for transparency and tax purposes. Your bank will convert to your local currency at the time of purchase — for most users, the displayed EUR price is close to the USD equivalent (€9.99 ≈ $10.80).",
              },
              "name": "Why is pricing in Euros instead of USD?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "No. All sales are final and we do not issue refunds under any circumstances, whether credits are used or unused. Purchased credits never expire, so you can use them whenever you're ready. If a restoration fails on our end, the credit is not deducted from your balance.",
              },
              "name": "Can I get a refund on unused credits?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "We don't deduct credits for failed restorations. If the result doesn't meet your expectations, you can try again on the same photo, try a different scan or version of the photo, or contact support. AI face restoration works best on portraits with clearly visible faces — heavily damaged or non-face photos may be limited.",
              },
              "name": "What if a restoration doesn't look good?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Credits are tied to the account that purchased them, but there's no limit on how many photos from different sources you can restore. A single Growth pack (60 credits) is enough for a whole family's photo archive.",
              },
              "name": "Can I share credits with family members?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
