  "/vs/myheritage": {
    "jsonLd": [
      {
        "data": {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@type": "FAQPage",
          "mainEntity": [
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "If you only need photo restoration, Magic Memory is the better choice. It is a standalone tool built specifically for restoring old photos using GFPGAN AI. MyHeritage bundles photo enhancement into a full genealogy subscription, which is significantly more expensive if photo restoration is all you need.",
              },
              "name": "Is Magic Memory or MyHeritage better for photo restoration?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Magic Memory offers one-time credit packages starting at €9.99 for 20 restorations, and the credits never expire. Unlimited use of MyHeritage Photo Enhancer comes with the MyHeritage Photo subscription, or a plan that includes it, and renews until you cancel. If you only have a few photos to restore, one-time credits usually cost less.",
              },
              "name": "How much does MyHeritage photo restoration cost vs Magic Memory?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Yes, MyHeritage stores photos in your account as part of its family tree features. Magic Memory does not persistently store any uploaded or restored photos — images are processed in memory and discarded after restoration.",
              },
              "name": "Does MyHeritage store my photos?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Technically yes, but the photo enhancement feature is locked behind a genealogy subscription. You would be paying for family tree tools, DNA matching, and historical records that you may not need. Magic Memory is purpose-built for photo restoration only.",
              },
              "name": "Can I use MyHeritage just for photo restoration?",
            },
            {
              "@type": "Question",
              "acceptedAnswer": {
                "@type": "Answer",
                "text": "Both produce good results for face restoration. Magic Memory uses GFPGAN, a research-grade model from CVPR 2021 specifically designed for face restoration. MyHeritage uses its own proprietary model. For most old family photos, both deliver noticeable improvement.",
